hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15604","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim informed me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah, from Muharrish al-Kabi, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left al-Jiranah at night when evening came, performing Umrah, and entered Makkah at night, and completed his Umrah, then left during that same night, and by morning he was at al-Jiranah as one who had spent the night, until when the sun declined he left al-Jiranah in the valley of Sarif until the road joined the road to Madinah at Sarif. Muharrish said: therefore his Umrah was hidden from many of the people."
